    "faceClearance": {
      "_about": "Captions never sit on his face. The caption band is fixed for the whole video (one template position per track), so the layout keeps his mouth above it: his lower lip's lowest point must be at least lowerLipToBandTopPx above the band's top. Band rows are the pill's as rendered in run 3 (two lines y 1372 to 1571, one line 1424 to 1521). Plan for two lines: lowest lower lip y 1252 in every layout. With a panel above him whose bottom edge is at y P, his eyes sit P + headroom below it and his lower lip a further eye-to-lip distance d (both in frame pixels at that framing), so the panel must end at or above y 1252 - headroom - d; at run 3's headroom (315) and face sizes (d 230 to 330) that is y 607 to 707. A panel ending lower needs his face smaller, or no face under it. Threshold from run 3 and run 2's cuts against the cold judge's 'captions over mouth or nose' rows: every judged frame had the band within 113 px of the lower lip, every passed frame 130 px or more. Measured with poc/hillclimb/C-work/scripts (mouth.swift, caption_rows.py, caption_face_overlap.py). Added 26 Oct by Claude Opus 5.5 (look and layout, hill-climb stream C).",
